---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { REPO_ROOT } from '../lib/github';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="About | printablestarcharts"
  description="Project framing and intended product shape for printablestarcharts."
>
  <section class="container prose-block">
    <p class="eyebrow">/ about</p>
    <h1>About printablestarcharts</h1>
    <p>
      printablestarcharts is intended to generate highly readable astronomy
      charts that still work in the field under red light, with printable PDFs
      as the primary output.
    </p>
    <p>
      The current repo is only a scaffold. It establishes the main worktree,
      Astro structure, and product docs so future implementation threads can
      build the actual chart-generation experience without redoing setup.
    </p>
    <p>
      Planned requirements live in the root docs, and source will eventually
      live on <a href={REPO_ROOT} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .prose-block {
    padding: 5rem 0;
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
</style>
